  "narrative": "All estimates are already signed to the registered direction. For direction -1, a positive signed estimate means a raw exposed-minus-comparator difference that is more negative, i.e. stronger dependency. I used approximate absolute comparator means and a 10% relative threshold; dependency scores are negative, so magnitude was taken as absolute. H13 and H14 both show strong, robust feature_065 associations within the complementary feature_034 strata: signed +0.106 and +0.128, corresponding to raw approx -0.106 and -0.128 stronger dependency in feature_065=1. Relative to approximate comparator means, these are roughly 40-50% stronger dependency, and both lower confidence bounds remain well above 10%, so multiplicity is unlikely to overturn them. Therefore H13 and H14 are accepted as within-dataset subgroup-specific associations and closed. H15 tests formal effect modification by feature_034; the signed interaction is -0.022, implying a raw interaction of approx +0.022, opposite the registered direction and small. The raw interval still includes clinically meaningful interaction values, so I do not accept or reject effect modification; investigation is closed because H13/H14 are similar and there is no compelling signal to pursue this exact interaction further. Cross-outcome feature_065 tests are mostly null. H16 outcome_001 and H17 outcome_006 have tiny signed estimates approx +0.009 and +0.004, raw approx -0.009 and -0.004, but their wide intervals include borderline clinically meaningful values and outcome_006 has a small mean, making relative thresholds unstable; they remain unresolved but deferred. H19 outcome_011 is opposite-trivial: signed -0.007 and the favorable upper bound corresponds to only about 7% relative dependency change, below the 10% threshold, so it is rejected for the registered direction. H18 outcome_014 is the most interesting secondary result: signed +0.032, raw approx -0.032 stronger dependency, about 37% relative to a small approximate comparator mean, but the interval includes zero and is wide because outcome_014 is dispersed and near zero on average; it is unresolved but active as a possible secondary association. H20 tests feature_054 level_001 vs level_002 for outcome_013; signed -0.013 means raw +0.013 in the opposite direction, and even the favorable upper bound is far below 10%, so it is rejected. Overall, feature_065 remains strongly associated with outcome_013 and is not clearly associated with the other tested outcomes, except possibly outcome_014. I do not request validation here because H7 was already independently validated and H13/H14 are pre-specified robustness checks of that validated association, not new independent biomarker claims. All conclusions are within-dataset associations only; no causal interpretation or generalizability is claimed. Opaque predictor labels also prevent ruling out leakage or confounding by correlated features.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 2 appraise updates: H13 and H14 accepted/closed; feature_065 effect on outcome_013 is meaningful in both feature_034=1 and feature_034=0 strata, with lower bounds >10% relative threshold. H15 unresolved/closed: formal feature_034 interaction is small/opposite but interval too wide to prove absence of modification; low priority. Cross-outcome scope: outcome_001 and outcome_006 near-null but imprecise, deferred; outcome_011 rejected for registered direction; outcome_014 remains active as possible secondary association but not accepted. H20 outcome_013 feature_054 main effect rejected. No validation requested because H7 already validated and subgroup follow-up largely confirms main association. Next priorities: test main effect of feature_034 on outcome_013; test whether feature_054 modifies feature_065 effect on outcome_013; follow outcome_014 feature_065 signal with targeted interaction if selected."
